      "textEn": "423\n\nNedurmuhurdundubhayah Sahasrasho\nGandharvakimpurushkinnarajagu. Mansvinaen kritam sudushkaram\nVidvanadadyadripave jagattrayam. 20>. Meaning of the word:\n\nNedhudu—Started playing; Muhudu—Again and again; Dundubhis—Drums; Sahasrashah—Hundreds; Gandharva—Dwellers of the Gandharva world; Kimpurusha—Dwellers of the Kimpurusha world; Kinnaras—Dwellers of the Kinnara world; Jagu—Started singing; Manasvina—By a very venerable person; Aneen—By the sacrifice; Kritam—Done; Su-dushkaram—Extremely difficult task; Vidwan—Because of being a scholar; Adat—Given as a donation; Yat—That; Ripave—To the enemy, Vishnu, who favors the enemies of Bali Maharaja; Jagat-trayam—The three worlds. Gandharvas, Kimpurs, and Kinnaras played thousands of drums again and again, and being very pleased,\nstarted singing, \"Bali Maharaj, how great a man is he, and how difficult a task he has accomplished.\"\nHe has done. Although they knew that Lord Vishnu was on the side of their enemies, even then they\ngave the entire three worlds in charity to God.\n\"\n\nThat which is beyond that form, which is wondrously increasing,\nThat which is the embodiment of the infinite qualities of Hari. Earth, sky, directions, heaven, earth,\nThe earth, gods, sages, when they exist. 21. Meaning of the word\n\nTat—That; Vamanam—the incarnation of Lord Vamana; Rupam—form; Avardhata—began to grow; Adbhutam—wonderful; Hareh—of the Lord; Anantasya—of the infinite; Guna-traya-atmakam—whose body is endowed with three qualities, expanded by material power;\nBhu—Earth; Kham—Sky; Dishah—All directions; Dyauh—Light; Vivaraah—Various openings of the universe; Payodhaah—Great ocean; Tiryak—Lower animals, birds; Nru—Humans; Devaah—Deities; Rishayah—Sages; Yat—In which; Asat—Dwelling; Aasata—Dwelling; Aasatah—Dwelling; Aasatah—Dwelling; Aasatah—Dwelling; Aasatah—Dwelling; Aasatah—Dwelling; Aasatah— Then the infinite God, who had assumed the form of Vamana, in terms of physical power,\nbegan to grow in size,