      "textEn": "426\n\nNurukramasyaorasi chakshamalam. 24). Meaning of the word\n\nSandhyam—Evening; Vibho—Of the Supreme God; Vasasi—In clothes; Guhye—In the secret parts; Aikshat—He saw; Prajapatin—Various\nPrajapatis, who gave birth to all living beings; Jaghane—On the hips; Atma-Mukhyan—Belonging to the trusted ministers of King Bali;\nNabhyam—On the navel; Nabhah—The entire sky; Kukshi-Sus—In the waist; Sapta—Seven; Sindhun—Of the oceans; Urukramasya—Of the Lord who\nwas performing wonderful deeds; Urasi—On the chest; Cha—Also; Riksha-Malam—A group of stars..\n\nBali Maharaj saw Sandhya under the clothes of the Lord who performs wonderful deeds, in their\nprivate parts, and in the round part of their waist, he saw himself and\nhis trusted councilors. He saw the sky in the navel of God, the seven seas in the waist, and\nall the groups of stars in his chest. Heart-dwelling, the dharma, the breasts, the moon -\nIn time, in truth, the mind's moon.\nWith a beautiful and radiant lotus-like face,\nAnd with ornaments adorning the neck. 25. In the ears of Indra, in the lotus-like feet,\nIn the ears, in the sky, in the head. In the hair, the cloud-like eyebrows,\nIn the eyes, the sun's face, and in the fire. 26. Vanyans chandansi rase jalesham\nBhruvonishhedam cha vidhi cha pakshmasu. Oh, night and day, and other men,\nMany are greedy for the forehead. 27). Touching the work of kings, the sandalwood is mixed.\nOn the back, in the order of righteousness, the sacrifice. Shadow, death, and laughter, and illusion,\nTanuruheshvoshadhijatayah. 2. Rivers, arteries, rocks, nails,\nBuddha, gods, sages, and others.\nIn the bodies of all beings, moving and still,\nHe is seen by all beings as a hero. 29. Meaning of the word:\n\nHridi—within the heart; Anga—hey king Parikshit; Dharmam—of Dharma; Stanyoih—on the breasts; Murarih—of Murari; Ritam—extremely sweet; Cha—also; Satyam—to the truth; Cha—also; Manasi—in the mind; Ath—thereafter; Indhum—to the moon; Shriyam—to Lakshmi;\nCha—a