र उनके शरीर के सारे बालों पर\nओषधियाँ तथा लताएँ थीं। उनकी नाड़ियों में सारी नदियाँ, उनके नाखूनों में सारे पत्थर, उनकी\nबुद्धि में ब्रह्माजी, देवता तथा महान् ऋषिगण और उनके सारे शरीर तथा इन्द्रियों में सारे जड़\nतथा चेतन जीव थे। इस प्रकार बलि महाराज ने भगवान् के विराट शरीर में प्रत्येक वस्तु को\nदेखा।\n\nसर्वात्मनीदं भुवनं निरीक्ष्य\nसर्वेऽसुराः कश्मलमापुरङ्ग ।\nसुदर्शनं चक्रमसह्यतेजो\nधनुश्च शार्ङ्गं स्तनयित्नुघोषम् ॥ ३०॥\n\nशब्दार्थ",
      "textEn": "\nMayam—to Maya; Tanuruheshu—on the body's hair; Oshadhi-jatayah—all kinds of herbs; Cha—and; Nadih—rivers; Chalishu—in the bones; Buddhau—in the intellect; Ajam—to Brahma; Deva-ganan—to the gods; Rishin cha—to the sages; Praneshu—in the senses; Gatre—in the body; Sthir-jangamani—to the inert and conscious;\nSarvani—all; Bhutani—to the living beings; Dadarsha—seen; Veera—by the brave; Bali Maharaj.. He saw in the heart of Lord Murari, Dharma, sweet words on the chest, and truth, in the mind,\nthe moon, Lakshmiji with lotus flowers in her hand on her chest, all the Vedas and all the sounds in her throat,\nall the gods, Indra etc. in her arms, all directions in both ears, the high realm on her head,\nclouds in her hair, air in her nostrils, the sun in her eyes, and saw the fire in her mouth.\nFrom his words, all\nVedic mantras were emerging, on his tongue was the water god Varundev, on his eyebrows was the rule-\nrule, and on his eyelids was day and night (day when eyes are open and night when closed). There was anger on his forehead and greed on his lips. Your Highness! In their touch, there were desires,\nIn their semen, all the water, on their back, unrighteousness, in their wonderful deeds or steps, there was the fire of Yagya.\nWas. In their shadow was death, in their smile was illusion, and on all the hair of their body\nthere were medicines and vines. In their veins were all the rivers, in their nails were all the stones, in their\nintellect was Brahmaji, gods, and great sages, and in their entire body and senses were all inert\nand conscious beings. In this way, Bali Maharaj saw every object in the immense body of God.\nSee. Having observed the entire world with all its consciousness,\nAll the demons are in a state of confusion. Sudarshanam chakramasahyatejo\nDhanushcha sharangam stanayitnughosham. 30>. Lexicon"
