      "textEn": "42\n\nSarva-atmani—in the supreme being or God; Idam—this universe; Bhuvanam—the three worlds; Nirikshya—by looking; Sarve—all;\nAsurah—demons, associates of Bali Maharaj; Kashmalam—lamentation; Aapuha—obtained; Anga—Oh King; Sudarshanam—Sudarshan\nnamed; Chakram—wheel; Anahata—unbearable; Tejah—heat; Dhanu—bow; Sharangam—named Sharanga; Stanayitnu—\nThe sound of surrounding clouds; Ghosham—sounds like. Your Highness! When all the demon followers of Maharaj Bali saw the immense form of God,\nwho had contained everything within his body, and when they saw the Sudarshan Chakra in the hands of God,\nwhich produces unbearable heat, and when they heard the clamorous sound of his bow, then due to all these things, sorrow arose in their hearts. The sound of rain, the water, the five-colored one.\nThe lotus, the Vishnu's mace, the swan.\nVidyadharo Asiha Shatachandra Yukta-\nStunuttamaavakshayasayakaau cha. 31. Meaning of the word:\n\nParjanya-ghosha: - Thunder-like roar; Jalajah: - God's conch; Panchajanya: - One named Panchajanya; Kamodaki: - One named Kamodaki; Namaka: - One named Namaka; Vishnu-gada: - One named Vishnu's mace; Tarasvini: - One named extremely fast; Vidyadhara: - One named Vidyadhara; Asi: - One named sword; Shat-chandra-\nYukta: - A shield adorned with hundreds of moons; Tunu-uttama: - One named best sword; Akshayasayaka: - One named Akshayasayaka; Cha: - One more..\n\nThe conch named Panchajanya of Lord, which makes a sound like clouds, extremely fast,\nA mace named Kamodaki, a sword named Vidyadhara, a shield adorned with hundreds of moon-like symbols,\nAnd the best among the swords, Akshayasayak—all of these appeared together to praise God. Sunandamukhya Upatasturisham\nParshadamukhyah Sahalokapala. Spuratkiritangadamkunalah\nSrivatsaratottamamekhalabarairah. 32. Madhu Vratastragvanamalavruto\nRarajanbhagavanurakramah.\nBy the feet, by the strength of the arms,\nBy the sky, by the body, by the directions, by the arms. 33. Meaning of 