ree worlds, falls into the abode of the Supreme Being.\nThe fame of the Lord is spread throughout the three worlds. 4>. Meaning of the word\n\nDhatu: - of Brahmaji; Kamandalu: - water from the Kamandal; Tat: - that; Urukramasya: - of Lord Vishnu; Pada-Avanija: - of the lotus feet of Lord Vishnu; Pavitrataaya: - by washing the lotus feet of Lord Vishnu and thus becoming divinely pure; Nara-Indra: - O King; Swadhuni: -\nThe river named Swadhuni of the divine world; Abhut: - became; Nabhasi: - in the outer sky; Sa: - that; Patati: - falling down; Nimarshi: -\nPurifying; Loka-Trayam: - the three worlds; Bhagavata: - of the Lord; Vishada: - so much; Iva: - as; Kirti: - fame or\nVictorious activity. Your Highness! The water that came out of Brahma's kamandal (water pot) started washing the lotus feet of Urukram Bhagwan, who performs wonderful deeds.\nHe started washing the lotus feet of Vamandev. In this way, this water became so pure that it\ntransformed into Ganges water, flowing down from the sky, and began to purify the three worlds, as if\nGod's pure glory."
